xpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:14:35-08:00","id":3508,"title":"","content":"The Deathlords are left suitably vague that they could make for good chronicle-fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/759-willr","name":"WillR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T09:12:04-08:00","id":3555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=3496#post3496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any gameline <i>needs</i> a Chronicle book of its own, <b>Geist</b> would be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And maybe a couple support books, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T13:07:49-08:00","id":3711,"title":"","content":"I'm working on it, so you'll have to wait and see (or dig through the old forums for my posts before they're gone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=3307#post3307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">rules for how exactly the ghosts grow in Rank...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in there. Actually, semi-preview time.<br /> <br /> By crossing Rivers. Every time a Ghost goes Rank Rivers deeper into the Underworld it gains a Rank. But every time it crosses a River it risks loosing Integrity. The deeper parts of the Underworld are full of Ghosts of enormous power, and no humanity at all.<br /> <br /> A word to the wise, do not cross the 11th River unless you know the Old Laws protect you from Ghosts. (Kerberoi get stronger even faster than Ghosts)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T13:59:05-08:00","id":3734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=3477#post3477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like a chronicle that focuses heavily on EITHER Abmortals or Sacrosanct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are crying out for expansion - a book, a chapter in a book... But an entire chronicle? They're too rare and individual to be major drivers on Sin-Eater society without a lot of reworking. The more obvious directions are the (boringly obvious) ghosts, geists and kerberoi. In that order, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:26:05-08:00","id":3839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=3711#post3711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on it, so you'll have to wait and see (or dig through the old forums for my posts before they're gone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you're not working on \u201cit\u201d; you\u2019re working on <i>your take</i> on it. It won\u2019t truly be <b>Geist</b>\u2019s Chronicle book until Onyx Path publishes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:12:12-08:00","id":4099,"title":"","content":"The Deathlords. Hands down. Not only are they hinted at being Cosmic-Tier Geists, but it also gives an option to redifine the social structure. So Requiem had a city and an ST driven mythos behind it, but Strix adds in a stalking, &quot;ephemeral&quot; predator that eats you, and then the book <i>looks at how your society adapts</i>. What if the Deathlords weren't just crazy freaky things dwelling in the depth of the (almost said Labyrinth &gt;.&lt;) Underworld, but things that governed and ruled by proxy.<br /> <br /> If Demons are spies, and Mages are (going to be) detectives, what if Geists were Soldiers? Or even better, Rebels?<br /> <br /> So much potential to go back into the pathos (in the literary sense) of Wraith with some of the same cWoD goth punk atmosphere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":667,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","user":"ABenniton","date":".  Clarity 11-06-2013, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:27:11-08:00","id":4294,"title":"","content":"I want a greater explanation of the Geist; what role it serves, how to use it in play, all that good stuff.<br /> <br /> My group has always ran with the Geist as a slightly more morally ambiguous, alien Shadow, and we even went so far as to include the practice of Shadowguiding (Geistguiding?), having someone else at the table play the eerie, morbid thing inside your head. Guidelines for what the Geist should be like (we've had everything from &quot;the embodiment of wanting to get every high you can out of life before you die&quot; to &quot;a greedy grave-robber who wishes to lord over the dead through artifacts,&quot;) and greatly enjoyed what the Geist brought to the table. The horror of Synergy needs to be played up.<br /> <br /> A greater purpose for Sin-Eaters would be great as well. The core book presents them as somewhere between members of a street gang, psychic mediums, Ghostbusters, and street-level superheroes. A greater focus on plumping the depths of the Underworld and perhaps expanding the repertoire of the Sin-Eater to encompass dealing with affronts to the natural balance of life and death (Vampires are dead yet still walk, the Reanimated are both desecrations of a dead body and a potentially new soul being brought into reality, zombies, necromancers, maybe even the Strix if you do crossover games) would be most desirable. As it stands, Sin-Eaters basically run around punching ghosts who step out of line, helping those who need to pass on, and sort of dicking around in pursuit of power. Helping them become more of a 'keepers of the balance' would give the game a wider focus.<br /> <br /> They need a larger variety of enemies; ghosts and ghosts only gets old after a while. They need more shock from their death and deal with their Geist, rather than how benign things become due to the current vagueness.<br /> <br /> I adore Geist; I've played in three chronicles over the past four years (though one of them was spent playing a Changeling, but I was co-Storyteller on that one) and loved them all equally. Geist came out at a bad time and suffered from not hitting enough points for people to really &quot;get it.&quot; I'd love to see it get the second chance (hah!) that it deserves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:22:15-08:00","id":4400,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the writers of GMC mentioned that it was tailor-made to support a Kerberoi Chronicles book for Geist. That's what I've been calling it (though the name bothers me. . . the Care-Bear-oy. . . )<br /> <br /> I actually think Geist is a pretty solid game in-and-of itself, I don't think it needs massive overhauls in terms of revamping Manifestations, like B&amp;S does with Disciplines. I'd like a little more detail about how, exactly Bound go about their work of Sin-Eating, what the options for dealing with ghosts are, and what the benefits and drawbacks of each one are. I'd also like more facility for Bound to actually deal with the world of the living. As it stands, the main ways they have of advancing as characters and regaining Plasm involve dealing with ghosts, which is all well and good, but what happens when a Bound doesn't want to deal with ghosts, or there aren't that many ghosts around?<br /> <br /> I'd also like more detail on how the Bound and her Geist interact. A lot of that has been filled in by players, but I'd really like to see more detail on that relationship, being as it's pretty much fundamental to the game, even more so than a Kindred and her Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:24:26-08:00","id":4403,"title":"","content":"I remember Geist having some funny antagonists that never got described. Cthonians, I think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:18:35-08:00","id":4476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=4400#post4400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, one of the writers of GMC mentioned that it was tailor-made to support a Kerberoi Chronicles book for Geist. That's what I've been calling it (though the name bothers me. . . the Care-Bear-oy. . . )</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's pronounced Cur-Bur-Oi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=4403#post4403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Geist having some funny antagonists that never got described. Cthonians, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fullest treatment those have gotten was in Mage: Summoners, with a bit of elaboration in Imperial Mysteries (Cthonians run the gamut from Ranks 1-6, take the forms of grief, decay, and horror, and all have power over death), though word from Dave is that the Lifeless creature summoned by one of Mummy's Utterances is a cthonian as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I prefer the &quot;ghosts that have lost any remnant of humanity&quot; theory or the &quot;natives of the Underworld&quot; theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-06-2013, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:59:47-08:00","id":4500,"title":"","content":"I personally see Cthonians as literally meaning &quot;It's a Death thingy but fuck me if I know&quot;; that is they probably aren't all the same kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:50:11-08:00","id":4675,"title":"","content":"To the extent that they have a unifying identity, it appears to be \u201cephemeral beings that are <i>not</i> ghosts, but still belong to ghostly Twilight and the Underworld\u201d. If <b>Geist</b> keeps the notion that a geist became what it is by consuming a spirit of Death, the problem of the now-separate Twilights that keep ghosts and spirits from even <i>interacting</i>, let alone consuming each other, could be resolved by saying that \u201cspirit of Death\u201d is another way of saying \u201cchthonian\u201d. OTOH, there have been hints that in the new \u201cehemeral beings\u201d rules, \u201cgeist\u201d is intended to mean \u201cghost of Rank 3+\u201d \u2014 which I consider boring in comparison, but which also resolves said dilemma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:36:25-08:00","id":4743,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, in GMC's ephemeral entities rules, Geists are Rank 3+ Ghosts. But so are Kerberoi, and they're <i>not</i> the same thing. I figure it branches.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T19:18:47-08:00","id":4791,"title":"","content":"Personally I think that following the threads of lost Tier 3 Krewes would be a great plot motivator, but I'm a sucker for world-spanning conspiracy and archaeology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> </div> Audentis Fortuna iuvat.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/548-generalvostok","name":"generalvostok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar548_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T18:59:53-08:00","id":6541,"title":"","content":"I have a funny fascination with the Tier system used in Hunter/GMC and want to see examples of krewes at each Tier, including the mythical Tier 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T20:36:15-08:00","id":6581,"title":"","content":"While I understand what they were going for, I think the complete absence of ready-made Krewes was a mistake; and I\u2019d like the Chronicle book to feature a few if only for use in the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T03:12:54-08:00","id":6712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dataweaver:<br /> Who or what should be the \u201cplot motivator\u201d (e.g., God-Machine, Strix, Idigam, Fallen World)? </div> </div> </div>The most obvious answer is something intruding from the Underworld, being it Deathlords or Chthonians, but the Strix and the Idigam are already about intrusions. So maybe Geist should be about something else.<br /> <br /> The Geist mythos is materialistic. Everything is solid in the underworld, and the setting abounds with enchanted objects; the Bound themselves are materialist in the other sense, often using their knowledge and position for profit.<br /> Sin-Eater society is trashy and iconoclastic, the Bound putting together their mythoi from whatever they fancy, with little regard for history or sanctity. The tier 3 krewes are a thing of the past.<br /> <br /> Or are they?<br /> <br /> <b>ABenniton</b> cites the suggestion that the Deathlords are epic level geists - but what if instead they're epic level <i>sineaters</i>? The old krewes are still around, and they <i>are</i> the Deathlords, engaged in a long game to wrest control of the Underworld from the Kerberoi? (And maybe rule the living world for good measure). The classical channels are taken - sineaters who follow them get suborned or eliminated - that's why the ones who survive are the ones who DIY their spirituality.<br /> <br /> So the game becomes learning this and deciding what to do about it. If anything - after all, maybe sineaters ruling the Underworld is better - but maybe different sineaters (like us) doing so is even better still. You find out there is a Man, and now you need to decide - quickly - whether to fight him, serve him, avoid him, or become him.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe it's less a conspiracy as such, and more a kind of autopilot. Geists ought to be changed by their time connected to a sineater - and they're certainly changed by their inclusion in a powerful krewe mythology. So instead of an active malign conspiracy, you have the what amounts to the ghost of a conspiracy, pursuing power and influence that's wielded blindly in the service of goals and ideologies that no longer apply to the world. The sineaters' usual job writ large.<br /> <br /> Either way, the second chance becomes something they don't just have, but something they can offer to individuals - living and dead - and to the world at large. (Even if nothing else I suggested suits, this last paragraph is what I feel most strongly should drive the book).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T03:45:32-08:00","id":6719,"title":"","content":"Whatever the plot motivator of Geist is; it has to do two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Be relevant on both sides, Life and Death. Earth and Underworld. The whole theme is about having one foot in each world (even more than Werewolves, Geists have far more ties to mortal society).<br /> 2) Work for all the Archetypes. It's got to work for a Necromancer delving underworld lore and a Celebrant who just wants to party. Professional ghostbusters and professional accountants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's why I think the plot motivator is the Geist. Life or Death, party or accountant. The Geist is the one thing that's always with you, and it can be customised to fit any plot. Your Geist could be pushing you to reclaim the Underworld from day one or point you to the best rums for the party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:17:50-08:00","id":7023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=6712#post6712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The most obvious answer is something intruding from the Underworld, being it Deathlords or Chthonians, but the Strix and the Idigam are already about intrusions. So maybe Geist should be about something else.<br /> <br /> The Geist mythos is materialistic. Everything is solid in the underworld, and the setting abounds with enchanted objects; the Bound themselves are materialist in the other sense, often using their knowledge and position for profit.<br /> Sin-Eater society is trashy and iconoclastic, the Bound putting together their mythoi from whatever they fancy, with little regard for history or sanctity. The tier 3 krewes are a thing of the past.<br /> <br /> Or are they?<br /> <br /> <b>ABenniton</b> cites the suggestion that the Deathlords are epic level geists - but what if instead they're epic level <i>sineaters</i>? The old krewes are still around, and they <i>are</i> the Deathlords, engaged in a long game to wrest control of the Underworld from the Kerberoi? (And maybe rule the living world for good measure). The classical channels are taken - sineaters who follow them get suborned or eliminated - that's why the ones who survive are the ones who DIY their spirituality.<br /> <br /> So the game becomes learning this and deciding what to do about it. If anything - after all, maybe sineaters ruling the Underworld is better - but maybe different sineaters (like us) doing so is even better still. You find out there is a Man, and now you need to decide - quickly - whether to fight him, serve him, avoid him, or become him.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe it's less a conspiracy as such, and more a kind of autopilot. Geists ought to be changed by their time connected to a sineater - and they're certainly changed by their inclusion in a powerful krewe mythology. So instead of an active malign conspiracy, you have the what amounts to the ghost of a conspiracy, pursuing power and influence that's wielded blindly in the service of goals and ideologies that no longer apply to the world. The sineaters' usual job writ large.<br /> <br /> Either way, the second chance becomes something they don't just have, but something they can offer to individuals - living and dead - and to the world at large. (Even if nothing else I suggested suits, this last paragraph is what I feel most strongly should drive the book).<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually played with this idea a bit when working on the Cosmic Tier equivalent for Sinnies for an archmaster game a friend of mine was running. The Bound (or the geist, potentially) had the choice of anchoring themselves to the UW as a whole at Psyche 6+ and ferrying a seed for a new Dead Dominion down into the Underworld. Benefits of getting access to some meta-level keys, although having a heavier tie to the Underworld could cut off dealings with the world above. Still working the kinks out of the idea, but it's been fun to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T20:06:07-08:00","id":7837,"title":"","content":"Deathlord Chronicle or Kerberoi Chronicle have nice rings to them.<br /> <br /> I definitely want to see a focused antagonist for Sin Eaters, a la the Strix or the Idigam or the... Fallen World?<br /> <br /> Yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T20:11:49-08:00","id":7840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=6712#post6712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>ABenniton</b> cites the suggestion that the Deathlords are epic level geists - but what if instead they're epic level <i>sineaters</i>? The old krewes are still around, and they <i>are</i> the Deathlords, engaged in a long game to wrest control of the Underworld from the Kerberoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to double check, and I did say that, but what I meant was more along the line of what you just said here: Deathlords as Cosmic Tier Geist line (which makes them Cosmic Sin-Eaters). I like the motivator being a war that plays out in different ways (in homage to the old Guild system of Oblivion and trying to wrest control of Stygia), but I don't think it should be Sin-Eaters-as-Deathlords v. Kerberoi because that's too easy to play off as the &quot;other&quot;. I feel that the Kereboi should be tools, employed by the Deathlords, as are other Geists, and ghosts, in a strange and Byzantine hierarchy building throughout history.<br /> So what then is the Motivation? Because what <b>The King's Raven</b> said is right: it has to be relevant to both sides, Living and Dead. So, why are all these Deathlords going to war with one another? The only answer I could easily propose is tacky at best: &quot;Souls&quot;.<br /> Each Deathlord, even each Dominion, is fueled and gains power from the souls within it. If each Horseman represents a Threshold, the Deathlords represent a specific type of death (electrocution in a puddle for instance), and each Deathlord uses this Byzantine power structure in order to complete their goals in the physical world, which in truth are elegantly simple: &quot;Get more deaths&quot;. (It also makes for a callous and terrible Quintessence alternative for a cosmic level Geist game.)<br /> So then the motivator is immediately relevant: what do you do when the Other-you tries to murder the people you love? Or the people that take care of you? Or your clients? And then the Sin-Eaters become these... thorns in the proverbial side of the powers that be, gaining power in order to combat the reality of the situation, all the while pied-pipering themselves into becoming the very thing they're fighting. Rebels in an endless war...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T23:56:36-08:00","id":7907,"title":"","content":"I could see a strong case being made (I may well type one later; I'm sleepy and confined to my tablet) for the krewe itself as the plot motivator. Put a greater focus on digging up the stories of ancient groups of Sin-Eaters and try to develop your krewe mythos, shale your own worldview. I really like that everyone has their own take on things, and think that a greater focus on that would ber really cool, much moreso than some big gribbly Underworld threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T02:01:07-08:00","id":7934,"title":"","content":"The whole war in the underworld concept completely misses the point of what Geist is about. A second chance at life. On the other hand atamajakki, &quot;the Krewe chronicles&quot; is something I could get behind. I've already written up a massive expansion in the importance of Krewe Mythology and Metaphysics. It was fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:51:22-08:00","id":8347,"title":"","content":"I disagree. If GMC taught us anything its that the plot motivator doesn't have to be engaged with. Sure, if you're a mortal, maybe the God-Machine's plans are messing with your life. But maybe you don't figure out the Infrastructure in time, and maybe you don't stop it. The messing around in your life though? It stops as the Infrastructure completes is goals and then is disassembled or left &quot;off&quot;. (A suitable scenario for a game that is supposed to be about occult mysteries and then the players end up more interested in interpersonal affairs.)<br /> <br /> In the same way: You're offered a second chance at life by the Bargain, and just like in the current version: you can totally ignore what your Geist tells you to do, or look at, or be a part of. You can take your mystical powers and do exactly whatever it is you want. In this hypothetical Chronicle book, you could even forge a Krewe mythos that doesn't deal <i>at all</i> with this war raging around you. But the fact is that things are trying to kill people in a very specific way. And you are these hapless people's only opportunity for a &quot;second chance&quot;.<br /> <br /> I will also be happy to admit that these ideas I've proposed do not take into account the Krewe, and I would definitely be interested in reading what a &quot;Krewe Chronicle&quot; would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T14:16:33-08:00","id":8364,"title":"","content":"Maybe the plot motivator dosn't have to be engaged with; but it does have to tie into the core theme of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T14:23:53-08:00","id":8368,"title":"","content":"Perhaps. How do the Strix tie in with the core theme of <b>Vampire</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T14:25:28-08:00","id":8369,"title":"","content":"Ask Rose; I don't know enough about Vampire.<br /> <br /> I'm sure they do though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:55:25-08:00","id":8430,"title":"","content":"The Geist as more than just a tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T17:34:28-08:00","id":8492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=8368#post8368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps. How do the Strix tie in with the core theme of <b>Vampire</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div> Quite easily. They're both the paranoia inherant in kindred society, amplified to an extreme, and they're fear of the Beast. Frenzy is a constant threat, of losing oneself to hunger and instinct, and the fear of diminishing Humanity is similar. Vampires cling to control of themselves; the Strix represent a complete loss of that, and it could happen to anyone, at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:03:35-08:00","id":9613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>atamajakki:</b><br /> I could see a strong case being made (I may well type one later; I'm sleepy and confined to my tablet) for the krewe itself as the plot motivator. </div> </div> </div>I agree. One of the reason's I've heard for the dearth of tier 3 krewes and trash-culture feel of present day sineaters is to allow PC krewes to bring about significant and lasting change in sineater society. Even if they don't, others will try to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Kings Raven:</b><br /> The whole war in the underworld concept completely misses the point of what Geist is about. A second chance at life. </div> </div> </div>This is why I brought up the notion of &quot;ghosts of krewes past.&quot; Rather than a malevolent conspiracy to be warred against, it's an echo written into the geists that were changed by serving as its channel. And since such an echo could only be carried through those geists, and geists are in their ideal state when bound to a sineater and walking both worlds, it naturally becomes something present in both worlds.<br /> <br /> But geists don't organise much by themselves, so on Earth it's going to be more like a pattern of Sacrosanct than a big enemy krewe. And yet it will pose many of the dangers of a big enemy krewe. Meanwhile, PC sineater society is the way it is because it's the isolated geists and the trash-culture Bound who are the ones who tend not to get sucked into those patterns of the past.<br /> <br /> But leftover channels of a dead conspiracy isn't a good way for geists to be. It's not good for the sineaters they're bound to. And it's not good for the humans or ghosts - or other sineaters - they steamroller over, either. So they have to be taken out. But taking them out really means laying them - just like ghosts. And giving them a second chance - just like the PC's have had.<br /> <br /> And that's something that could be at the heart of a krewe chronicle too.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:36:16-08:00","id":9625,"title":"","content":"I think I might steal that idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't see it as the heart of the Krewe Chronicles*, the heart should be the PC's own Krewe, not NPC Krewes. But for PCs looking for a place in the world (rather than, e.g. getting rich) interacting with the ghosts of people asking the same questions could be interesting. For Gatekeepers they're a great antagonist to fight. For Necromancers a cool mystery to study with the promise of new tricks as a reward.<br /> <br /> I'd have to think of how they work. Armies of Ghosts? Sin-Eater Pawns? A Tier 6 Geist with a hundred avatars? Still, it's cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I'm still not sure if I'm in favour of the Geist Chronicles or the Krewe Chronicles but looking at what I've written so far, it could support both. I've massively upgraded the importance of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T21:25:37-08:00","id":10187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=9613#post9613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree. One of the reason's I've heard for the dearth of tier 3 krewes and trash-culture feel of present day sineaters is to allow PC krewes to bring about significant and lasting change in sineater society. Even if they don't, others will try to.<br /> <br /> This is why I brought up the notion of &quot;ghosts of krewes past.&quot; Rather than a malevolent conspiracy to be warred against, it's an echo written into the geists that were changed by serving as its channel. And since such an echo could only be carried through those geists, and geists are in their ideal state when bound to a sineater and walking both worlds, it naturally becomes something present in both worlds.<br /> <br /> But geists don't organise much by themselves, so on Earth it's going to be more like a pattern of Sacrosanct than a big enemy krewe. And yet it will pose many of the dangers of a big enemy krewe. Meanwhile, PC sineater society is the way it is because it's the isolated geists and the trash-culture Bound who are the ones who tend not to get sucked into those patterns of the past.<br /> <br /> But leftover channels of a dead conspiracy isn't a good way for geists to be. It's not good for the sineaters they're bound to. And it's not good for the humans or ghosts - or other sineaters - they steamroller over, either. So they have to be taken out. But taking them out really means laying them - just like ghosts. And giving them a second chance - just like the PC's have had.<br /> <br /> And that's something that could be at the heart of a krewe chronicle too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of the Geist's... incongruities? (Not quite what I mean, but we'll go with it for now.) being accidental in nature. My only concern is that the implication becomes that getting together in a group becomes harmful if the group gets large enough, which leads to factionalism and, potentially, a desire for the PCs to not reach out to alter Sin-Eater society at the risk of damaging their own Geist, especially if they're so invested in providing a second chance for other Geists: they <i>know</i> the damage being a channel for a large enough krewe does to their Geist. My fear would be that in a product, as your idea stands, it would be terribly easy to slide into defeatism.<br /> <br /> I also can see the appeal in your idea of turning the game around to aim at providing <i>Geists</i> with second chances; but its not something that I would personally engage with (for what it's worth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T23:44:38-08:00","id":10243,"title":"","content":"Mechanical weight to the Bargain and the Geist's interests. You can argue &quot;the character doesn't know they don't have to serve their geist&quot; and &quot;a voice in your head would be pretty disturbing in its own right&quot; all you want - but the PLAYER doesn't feel that in any way. I'm not saying the Geist should be able to steal your character, but some mechanical leverage (offered beats? withholding dice? etc) with the character makes the Bargain a much more visceral experience for the PLAYER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-15-2013, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T02:44:11-08:00","id":10286,"title":"","content":"Hey Glamourweaver; welcome to the new forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I strongly agree with you; my system is to give a Geist a Virtue/Vice called Past/Passion. There's a second Geist-related Willpower pool that you can fill either by uncovering it's Past, resolving issues from it's past, or indulging it's wants. Depending on the player's choice that could result in an easy partnership, a Celebrant who's Geist has the Passion &quot;PARTY!&quot; or you could end up having a Murderous Geist which forces you to dig up it's Past for blackmail material.<br /> <br /> You use the new Willpower trait to auto-win conflicts with your Geist. This can prevent the Geist from taking over, or make the Geist use Manifestations for you.<br /> <br /> <br /> ABenniton, the simple solution is to say that only happens some times; and perhaps to say that it's not always harmful when it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:25:03-08:00","id":10294,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see a deeper description on Archetypes, and possibly what it means to be part of a given Thresolds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:32:06-08:00","id":10295,"title":"","content":"Another agreement. I've done a lot on Thresholds, I'm not really sure how to go deeper on Archetypes though... (apart from fixing Pilgrims)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:44:23-08:00","id":10557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=10286#post10286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Glamourweaver; welcome to the new forum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I strongly agree with you; my system is to give a Geist a Virtue/Vice called Past/Passion. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea a lot. Not 100% sure on where you're going with it, and it could really overcomplicate Sin-eaters if they have their own Vice/Virtue or equivalent as well, but... damn it's a great idea. for making the Geists history and attitudes <i>mechanically</i> important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T20:53:53-08:00","id":11039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=10286#post10286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ABenniton, the simple solution is to say that only happens some times; and perhaps to say that it's not always harmful when it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Personally, I feel that takes the teeth out of it though. I also had a brainstorm today, and thought that perhaps, instead of it being Tier 3 Krewes that cause a Geists... &quot;incongruities&quot; maybe it's being one of the Wretched that causes it. And maybe being a part of a Krewe and more at higher levels, is what helps insulate the Geists against the maddening effects of being set loose in the physical/Twilight world. Or perhaps even the &quot;Unbound&quot;: Geists that have not yet found a suitable host to offer the Bargain to. This does shift it towards being more of a Geist-Chronicle than a Krewe-Chronicle though.<br /> <br /> Also, I do love the Virtue/Vice replacement being Past/Passion. Although, if I may make a suggestion: instead of another expendable resource like Willpower, maybe something closer to Cover Beats and Cover Experiences from Demon, with Conditions that allow you to ignore (or force you to give in) to your Geist. In addition to having them refill your Willpower to varying degrees.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems like you're doing an awful lot of work, Raven, who else is writing this with you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T21:11:00-08:00","id":11045,"title":"","content":"Apologies if I'm reiterating what other folks have stated they wanted already;<br /> <br /> The Synergy system overhauled; the hierarchy of sins never made any sense to me to reflect much of the Geist/Sineater dynamic. Not enough focus on the individual Geist at all. It resembles an early draft artifact of the Sin-Eaters being a heavy Psychopomp type without the rest of the material really supporting it that well (by that I mean in presentation; resolving a ghosts issues is the best way to get plasm, but it gets such a TINY reference, and many of the archetypes don't quite jive with it). Needs fixing. It's been the most asynchronous &quot;morality&quot; I've ran into with the WoD line thus far, which is very odd.<br /> <br /> -Some mechanic to reflect the influence and impact of the Geist; mentioned plenty of times. It doesn't do enough for my tastes, but this is skewed in part due to my love of Wraith; I'd much prefer to see something like &quot;Shadow dice&quot; to reflect getting the cooperation of your Geist empowering you, but working against it actively posing more tangible issues. Synergy still doesn't quite do enough here.<br /> <br /> -More focus on the Geist itself; I didn't feel that reading and then playing the game. It feels utterly neutered and for all the spectacular things it gives the character, treated to much in presentation as an afterthought after it creates the Sin Eater. <br /> <br /> -Less blather about Spirit/Ghost hybrids; seriously, no. Treat them as their own thing, even if -sometimes- they -might- be the result of a ghost eating a spirit or vice versa. It's not very evocative, it doesn't really give them enough oomph. Since Book of the Dead, Mummy and even GMC, I think there's much more room to present these things as something interesting and unique. Tacking them off as some meta-mechanical hybrid doesn't really evoke how fucked up and interesting they are, let alone the potential they have. It feels too much like a major facet of the character is more of a meta-mechanic afterthought. We don't need justification for why these exist Out-of-Character because they weren't originally part of the other setting books; it should be enough that they do.<br /> <br /> -More emphasis and focus on the Archetypes; there's a consistent complaint that there's a lack of &quot;focus&quot; in the game I've gotten from my play-groups; until I started reading (and re-reading) Archetypes and just how important they are to -giving- your character that big Purpose with a capital P, I had the same issues. This is a -big- area of the game I didn't feel got presented as being as important as it is. Primarily this is a formatting issue; I think they need to be at the forefront more given they pretty much are the way to mould where your character is going, what they're doing and even a means of regaining Plasm.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head. I have the book, but only got to play it a couple of times and haven't since. We never got the chance to get the 1.1 version (missed out it seems on the, show your book, get it on Drive Thru thing that went some time back) when really that should have just been handed out as a free errata. Might have helped, but there's some things I definitely know I'd like to see stemming from what we ran into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T02:27:38-08:00","id":11129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABenniton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=11039#post11039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Personally, I feel that takes the teeth out of it though.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that so long as an individual &quot;Dead Krewe&quot; has plenty of teeth it won't matter so much if the system that creates them is a bit de-fanged.<br /> <br /> As I said earlier, to me &quot;Krewe Chronicles&quot; and &quot;Geist Chronicles&quot; would both mean &quot;My Krewe/Geist Chronicle&quot; so Dead Krewes and other Underworld nastys don't need to shoulder the weight of being the heart of the story. Just an interesting antagonist or at most an antagonist who serves as an interesting foil to your Krewe/Geist/Second Chance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABenniton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=11039#post11039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I do love the Virtue/Vice replacement being Past/Passion. Although, if I may make a suggestion: instead of another expendable resource like Willpower, maybe something closer to Cover Beats and Cover Experiences from Demon, with Conditions that allow you to ignore (or force you to give in) to your Geist. In addition to having them refill your Willpower to varying degrees.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't really want to use Geist Beats because I already have Krewe Beats. The ability to stockpile Geist-autowins is actually quite important to the whole system.<br /> <br /> Basically a quick summery: If you have high Synergy you get a larger stockpile of Geist-Willpower, a bonus on forcing your Geist to do stuff, but a <u>penalty</u> on resisting your Geist's attempts to seize control. The idea is that because you have this large stockpile the penalty will never matter, just spend points to auto-win every time.<br /> <br /> So basically; the idea is that high synergy makes it really easy to deal with your Geist but only if you actually role-play high Synergy by frequently using Passions and Past to keep that extra large stockpile topped up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABenniton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=11039#post11039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it seems like you're doing an awful lot of work, Raven, who else is writing this with you?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just me, and it is a lot of work (22000 words so far) so naturally it's slow going. I'm trying to focus mostly on mechanics since, in my opinion, the majority of the Geist fluff is already gold.<br /> <br /> Though it is encouraging when I read threads like this and see a lot of people asking for stuff I'm working on: More Geist focus/mechanics. Overhauled Synergy. Etc. I want to give more to Archetypes too, but I'm not really sure how (apart from making them more important for Plasm regeneration)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-15-2013, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:34:11-08:00","id":13045,"title":"","content":"You know what'd be hilarious and great as a SE plot or book or side-story, but wouldn't really work as a chronical? Miracle Day. Sin Eaters would be absolutely pissed if a Miracle Day situation happened. Sadly, that would affect the entire world.<br /> <br /> I think Tempest, Malestrom or Spectre Chronicles might be a good idea. Its a slight nod Wraith. Have the Tempest or whatever pour out of underworld gates into the real world, having some deleterious effects. Spectres would be personifications of that threat created or released by the Tempest. Inside the local underworld when the Tempest is raging is even worse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:59:20-08:00","id":13461,"title":"","content":"Eh. nWoD\u2019s cosmology doesn\u2019t include a Tempest, Maelstrom, or Spectres \u2014 though that <i>might</i> change at least somewhat, if and when nWoD gets an actual <b>Wraith</b> line. But for <b>Geist</b>? No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:16:18-08:00","id":71505,"title":"","content":"I would love a Geist Chronicle Book. Bring on the &quot;Kerberoi Chronicle!&quot; (or, y'know, something to that effect). And because I've just seen Dataweaver's post, anything's possible in the WoD. We could get a Wraith line, although it's more likely that since they're Deathly, and we already have 3 Deathly lines, most things Wraith related would probably just be fit into the Geist world. To Sin-Eaters &quot;Spectres&quot; could be the new Strix. Ahem, <b>Onyx Path</b>, take note! :-P<br /> <br /> Also, erm... <b>*bump*</b> :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/933-shadowhowler","name":"shadowhowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T16:26:33-08:00","id":71702,"title":"","content":"I would like to see some more explication on what Psyche is/means. The section on Psyche in the book states that Sin-Eaters with a high rating in it are avatars of Death, more or less, which carries some metaphysical implications for the link between Geist and Bound (that is to say, being Bound is more than just having a ghost in your head). I don't quite understand why Sin-Eaters with a high Psyche rating have to form anchors and spend time in the Underworld, beyond certain mythic ties and the fact that every Supernatural Resistance stat has drawbacks. There's also an implication that Psyche can be lowered; I'd like an expansion on that.<br /> <br /> I feel like the rules for Krewes, especially all the additional Merits, are serpentine and contradictory and could use some streamlining. Maybe do something with Mummy's Cult rules, the Mystery Cult Initiation Merit, etc. Also I think the Tiers need more evocative names than Cult, Faction, and Conspiracy (there are a couple of other Sin-Eater terms that feel equally flat &amp; uninspired, such as War Council).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T17:03:24-08:00","id":84930,"title":"","content":"Some of the mechanics do need...tweaking, to be sure. Synergy, for instance: I really think that would benefit from an Integrity-like system more than its current form. <i>Maybe</i> some sort of interaction between Psyche and Synergy, like when invoking Manifestations you get a modifier of Synergy - Psyche, or something (that's not even a little thought out) to illustrate the power and need to keep your Geist happy, otherwise it starts fighting you.<br /> <br /> But one thing I hope they don't change, in the event a book happens, much is the fluff. I really, really like the fluff for <b>Geist</b>, and while <b>B&amp;S</b> makes me a lot more confident than I was previously that they're not going to forcibly tie everything to the God-Machine, and they are absolutely capable of improving on things, well, I kind of like it as it is. Exploring some things in greater depth, sure. But there is the risk, albeit a small one, that by focussing more on, say, the Kerbori, they make them more of a central antagonist, and I'm cool with them just being those weird, powerful things that rule areas in the Underworld for...reasons. The Underworld is <i>important</i>, certainly, but <b>Geist</b> is, at its heart, a game about life and death, which means it mostly takes place in the land of the living with excursions to the Underworld. If it becomes more central, then in my opinion they risk undermining that.<br /> <br /> That said, they did a fantastic job of <b>B&amp;S</b>, so maybe I'm worrying about nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3073-second-chances-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-geist-s-chronicle-book?p=4743#post4743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, in GMC's ephemeral entities rules, Geists are Rank 3+ Ghosts. But so are Kerberoi, and they're <i>not</i> the same thing. I figure it branches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured Rank was a measure of power, but there's a vast difference in kind. A Rank 2 ghost and a Rank 2 spirit might be equally powerful, but they're not even remotely the same thing. So while a geist might be Rank 3+ in terms of power (and they are quite powerful), that doesn't necessarily imply that they're just strong ghosts. They're ghostly <i>and</i> spirit-y, but also something else...ly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T23:33:17-08:00","id":85137,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a Geist Chronicle book happen. I think it would really be a good thing for the line. Picking what to focus on may be tricky, but it would work out, I am sure.<br /> <br /> And yea, <b>B&amp;S</b> is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-06-2014, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T16:31:06-07:00","id":100944,"title":"","content":"A month later,I'd like to voice that it should be The Horsemen Chronicles.<br /> <br /> More on why and what I'd like to see later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attac